\DOC SUBSUMED_ID_MAYCHANGE_TAC

\TYPE {SUBSUMED_ID_MAYCHANGE_TAC : tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Closes goals stating that the identity relation is subsumed by a relation built
from {ASSIGNS} components, possibly combined with the sequencing operator.

\DESCRIBE
Takes no arguments. The goal must have the form {A ?- (=) subsumed t}, where
{t} is either a single {ASSIGNS} applied to a state component (including
composed components such as a register sub-field or a memory region), or a
chain of such {ASSIGNS} terms joined by the relation-composition operator. The
assumptions {A} are untouched and play no role; they may be absent or an
arbitrarily large context.
{
   A ?- (=) subsumed t
   =================== SUBSUMED_ID_MAYCHANGE_TAC
}

\FAILURE
Fails when the right-hand side of {subsumed} is not of the {ASSIGNS}-based form
handled — in particular when it is a differently shaped change relation — the
failure arising inside the tactic as an unsuccessful match of its implication
theorem against the conclusion; this occurs both with and without assumptions
present.

\COMMENTS
The observed traces show only this closing behaviour, never a transformed or
split goal.

\ENDDOC
